# The ledger of `image/colorspace`: what Go's `image/color` (Go 1.27, this
# machine's `go doc -all image/color`, 2026-11-23), Python's `colorsys`
# (Python 3.15, `dir(colorsys)` on this machine) and Pillow's colour modes
# let a program do with colours in other spaces than RGB, one block per
# capability, and what Rebel answers. Pillow is not installed here and
# nothing may be installed, so its names are those of its documented API,
# not read by `dir()`. Rust's standard library has no colour spaces: `-`.
#
# The expected values are observed: Go's integer conversions (CMYK and YCbCr
# both ways) by a Go program run on this machine over 5000 pseudo-random
# colours and the primaries, weighed by position so a single difference
# shows, and Python's `colorsys` (floats) on ten colours and the inverses of
# twelve, the hue turned to degrees.

capability colorspace/hsv  a colour as hue, saturation and value, both ways
  heroes  image/colorspace.Hsv, image/colorspace.to_hsv, image/colorspace.from_hsv
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  colorsys.rgb_to_hsv, colorsys.hsv_to_rgb, Image.convert("HSV")
  note    the hue in degrees where colorsys turns it to 0 up to 1, so a picker needs no scaling; the channels are 8-bit colours, and from_hsv rounds each to 8 bits. Black and grays have hue 0, as colorsys answers

capability colorspace/hls  a colour as hue, lightness and saturation, both ways
  heroes  image/colorspace.Hls, image/colorspace.to_hls, image/colorspace.from_hls
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  colorsys.rgb_to_hls, colorsys.hls_to_rgb
  note    CSS's `hsl()`, in colorsys's order of components (hue, lightness, saturation); the hue in degrees as under hsv

capability colorspace/cmyk  a colour as the inks of a printer, both ways
  heroes  image/colorspace.Cmyk, image/colorspace.to_cmyk, image/colorspace.from_cmyk
  go      color.CMYK, color.CMYKModel, color.RGBToCMYK, color.CMYKToRGB
  rust    -
  python  Image.convert("CMYK")
  note    Go's integer conversion, which Pillow's `convert("CMYK")` shares in effect: black is what the brightest channel lacks and each ink its channel's lack over the brightest, truncated. It is the naive conversion with no ink limit, no under colour removal and no profile, which a press needs (colour management is pending in `image`'s ledger)

capability colorspace/ycbcr  a colour as JPEG's brightness and colour differences, both ways
  heroes  image/colorspace.YCbCr, image/colorspace.to_ycbcr, image/colorspace.from_ycbcr
  go      color.YCbCr, color.YCbCrModel, color.RGBToYCbCr, color.YCbCrToRGB
  rust    -
  python  Image.convert("YCbCr")
  note    JFIF's equations in the 16-bit fixed point whose rows sum so that a gray has both differences at 128, rounded to the nearest and held to 0 up to 255, equal to Go's over every colour sampled

capability colorspace/yiq  a colour as NTSC's brightness and two colour axes, both ways
  heroes  image/colorspace.Yiq, image/colorspace.to_yiq, image/colorspace.from_yiq
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  colorsys.rgb_to_yiq, colorsys.yiq_to_rgb
  note    colorsys's coefficients; from_yiq holds the channels to 0 up to 255 as colorsys holds them to 0 up to 1

capability colorspace/planes  an image split into the planes of a space and put together again
  heroes  image/colorspace.Space, image/colorspace.split, image/colorspace.merge
  go      color.NYCbCrA, color.NYCbCrAModel
  rust    -
  python  Image.split, Image.merge
  note    each plane an 8-bit gray image, which is what Pillow's split answers for a colour mode; a plane is not a pixel format of `image`, whose eight formats stay as they are, so the colour is in the program's hand between a split and a merge. The hue plane is 0 up to 255 for 0 up to 360 degrees. A plane of Go's NYCbCrA (a YCbCr with alpha) is the three of `ycbcr` and `image`'s own alpha

capability colorspace/lab  the Lab and XYZ colour spaces
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.convert("LAB"), ImageCms
  note    -

dropped
  go      color.Color, color.Model, color.ModelFunc: interfaces and a function type, which the language has none of; a colour is `image.Color`
  go      color.RGBA, color.RGBA64, color.NRGBA, color.NRGBA64, color.Gray, color.Gray16, color.Alpha, color.Alpha16, color.Palette, color.RGBAModel, color.NRGBAModel, color.GrayModel, color.AlphaModel and the others of the colour models of RGB and gray: held by `image`'s ledger
  go      color.NYCbCrA's Palette and Index methods and color.Palette.Convert, color.Palette.Index: held by `image`'s palette block
  python  colorsys.ONE_THIRD, colorsys.ONE_SIXTH, colorsys.TWO_THIRD, colorsys.__all__: constants of colorsys's own arithmetic
